<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mwari cult</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mwari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mwari cult is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> religious tradition centred on the high god Mwari, with oracular shrines in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matopos-hills">Matopos Hills</a> of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> it provided ritual sanction and ideological legitimacy for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changamire">Changamire</a> rulers. Its priestly networks also served as a channel of communication and gift exchange between the court and the plateau's chiefly communities.</p></div>
